Actual source paths and scope:
- plugins/platforms/discord/adapter.py: DiscordAdapter.MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH,
  MAX_SPLIT_MESSAGES, _cap_split_chunks, send. text.rs adapts the small eight
  chunk cap algorithm: retain seven chunks and replace the remainder with a
  plain Anima truncation notice; complete reply remains in native session
  history. Splitting is rewritten in Rust, preserving Unicode scalar
  boundaries and additionally bounding each message to 2000 UTF-16 units.
  This conservative difference makes emoji-heavy replies use more chunks.
- plugins/platforms/discord/adapter.py: _build_allowed_mentions. client.rs
  adapts explicit mention suppression. Anima intentionally disables every
  ping class, including user/replied-user pings enabled by upstream defaults.
  There are no profile, config or environment override paths.
- plugins/platforms/discord/adapter.py: _discord_message_admission,
  _dispatch_recovered_message, _iter_missed_message_backfill_candidates,
  _advance_discord_recovery_cursor. Native client/inbound code adapts behavior
  and identities, selected-channel/sender checks, completed receipts and
  recovery cursor sequencing. Anima rejects bots/self/webhooks, uses an exact
  owner allowlist and proves a bounded backward REST scan before cursor
  movement. This is architectural/behavior reuse, not copied Python code.
- plugins/platforms/discord/recovery.py: DiscordRecoveryStore and messages/
  cursors schema. model.rs and Anima snapshots reuse recovery behavior only;
  SQLite schema, WAL/profile fallback and logging are not copied.
- plugins/platforms/discord/plugin.yaml: protocol/display metadata only.
- tests/gateway/test_discord_allowed_mentions.py,
  test_discord_bot_auth_bypass.py, test_discord_missed_message_backfill.py,
  test_discord_split_cap.py: relevant edge-case behavior informs native fake
  fixtures. No upstream tests or Python modules are executed.

Anima's adapter is a selected guild text-channel REST polling implementation.
It does not port upstream Gateway, threads, roles, multiplex profiles, voice,
formatting, config, installation or slash-command machinery; no adapter parity
is claimed. Credentials remain in Anima's independent generation-bound vault.

